Frontend Authentication Checklist
1. Sign-In/Sign-Up UI
[ ] A dedicated sign-in page (e.g., /auth/signin)
[ ] Buttons for OAuth providers (Google, GitHub)
[ ] (Optional) Email/password form if required by requirements
[ ] Clear branding and project name/logo
2. NextAuth Integration
[ ] NextAuth configured with all required providers
[ ] Sign-in page uses signIn() from next-auth/react
[ ] Handles redirect after successful login
3. User Feedback
[ ] Loading indicator during authentication
[ ] Error messages for failed logins (e.g., invalid credentials, OAuth errors)
[ ] Success message or redirect on successful login
4. Session Awareness
[ ] Show user info (avatar, name, email) when logged in (e.g., in navbar or dashboard)
[ ] Show sign-in/sign-up options when logged out
[ ] Sign-out button that calls signOut() from next-auth/react
5. Accessibility & UX
[ ] All buttons and forms are keyboard accessible
[ ] Proper ARIA labels for form fields and buttons
[ ] Responsive design for mobile and desktop
6. Security
[ ] No sensitive data in client-side code
[ ] No userId or tokens stored in localStorage (NextAuth handles this securely)
[ ] Only show authenticated content to logged-in users
7. Testing
[ ] Test login with each OAuth provider
[ ] Test error states (invalid login, canceled OAuth, etc.)
[ ] Test sign-out and session expiration